#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:6
msgid "sbt publish"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:9
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:12
msgid ""
"`sbt` \\[_query_ / \\] `publish`<br> `sbt` \\[_query_ / \\] "
"`publishSigned`<br> `sbt` \\[_query_ / \\] `publishLocal`<br> `sbt` \\"
"[_query_ / \\] `publishM2`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:17
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:20
msgid ""
"The publish family of tasks provide means for compiling and publishing your "
"project. _Publishing_ in this context consists of uploading a descriptor, "
"such as a Maven POM or `ivy.xml`, and artifacts, such as a JAR or `war` "
"file, to a repository so that other projects can specify your project as a "
"dependency."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:26
msgid ""
"The `publish` task publishes your project to a remote repository, such as "
"JFrog Artifactory or Sonatype Nexus instance."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:28
msgid ""
"The `publishSigned` task, enabled using [sbt-pgp plugin](https://github.com/"
"sbt/sbt-pgp), is used to publish GPG-signed artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:30
msgid ""
"The `publishLocal` task publishes your project to the Ivy local file "
"repository, which is usually located at `$HOME/.ivy2/local/`. You can then "
"use this project from other projects on the same machine."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:32
msgid ""
"The `publishM2` task publishes your project to the local Maven repository."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:34
msgid ""
"There's a specific recipe for [publishing to the Central Repo](../recipes/"
"central.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:36
msgid "Skip publishing"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:38
msgid ""
"To avoid publishing a project, add the following setting to the subprojects "
"that you want to skip:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:44
msgid "Common use case is to prevent publishing of the root project."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:46
msgid "Define the repository"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:48
msgid ""
"To specify the repository, assign a repository to `publishTo` and optionally "
"set the publishing style. For example, to upload to Nexus:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:52
msgid "\"Sonatype Snapshots Nexus\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:52
msgid "\"https://oss.sonatype.org/content/repositories/snapshots\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:55
msgid "To publish to a local maven repository:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:58
msgid "\"local-maven\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:58
msgid "\"path/to/maven-repo/releases\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:61
msgid "To publish to a local Ivy repository:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:64
msgid "\"local-ivy\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:64
msgid "\"path/to/ivy-repo/releases\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:67
msgid ""
"If you're publishing the Central Repository, you will also have to select "
"the right repository depending on your artifacts: SNAPSHOT versions go to "
"the central-snapshots repository while other versions go to the local "
"staging repository. Doing this selection can be done by using the value of "
"the `version` setting:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:75
msgid "\"https://central.sonatype.com/repository/maven-snapshots/\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:76
msgid "\"-SNAPSHOT\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:76
msgid "\"central-snapshots\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:81
msgid "Publishing locally"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:83
msgid ""
"The `publishLocal` task will publish to the \"local\" Ivy repository. By "
"default, this is at `$HOME/.ivy2/local/`. Other builds on the same machine "
"can then list the project as a dependency. For example, if the project you "
"are publishing has configuration parameters like:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:89
#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:97
msgid "\"com.example\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:90
#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:97
msgid "\"0.1-SNAPSHOT\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:91
#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:97
msgid "\"hello\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:94
msgid "Then another build on the same machine can depend on it:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:100
msgid ""
"The version number you select must end with `SNAPSHOT`, or you must change "
"the version number each time you publish to indicate that it's a changing "
"artifact."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:104
msgid ""
"```admonish warning\n"
"Generally the use of SNAPSHOT dependencies should be avoided beyond testing "
"on a single machine\n"
"since it makes dependency resolution slower and the build non-repeatable.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:109
msgid ""
"Similar to `publishLocal`, `publishM2` task will publish the user's Maven "
"local repository. This is at the location specified by `$HOME/.m2/"
"settings.xml` or at `$HOME/.m2/repository/` by default. Another build would "
"require `Resolver.mavenLocal` to resolve out of it:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:122
msgid "Credentials"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:124
msgid "There are two ways to specify credentials for such a repository."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:126
msgid "The first and better way is to load them from a file, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:129
msgid "\".sbt\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:129
msgid "\".credentials\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:132
msgid ""
"The credentials file is a properties file with keys `realm`, `host`, `user`, "
"and `password`. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:142
msgid "The second way is to specify them inline:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:145
msgid "\"Sonatype Nexus Repository Manager\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:145
msgid "\"my.artifact.repo.net\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:145
msgid "\"admin\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:145
msgid "\"admin123\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:148
msgid ""
"````admonish note\n"
"Credentials matching is done using both: `realm` and `host` keys.\n"
"The `realm` key is the HTTP `WWW-Authenticate` header's realm directive, "
"which is\n"
"part of the response of HTTP servers for [HTTP Basic Authentication](https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basic_access_authentication#Server_side).\n"
"For a given repository, this can be found by reading all the headers "
"received.\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"curl -D - my.artifact.repo.net\n"
"```\n"
"````"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:160
msgid "Cross-publishing"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:162
msgid ""
"To support multiple incompatible Scala versions, use projectMatrix and "
"publish (see [Cross building setup](./cross-building-setup.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:165
msgid "Overriding the publishing convention"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:167
msgid ""
"By default sbt will publish your artifact with the binary version of Scala "
"you're using. For example if your project is using Scala 2.13.x your example "
"artifact would be published under `example_2.13`. This is often what you "
"want, but if you're publishing a pure Java artifact or a compiler plugin "
"you'll want to change the `CrossVersion`. See the [Cross building setup](./"
"cross-building-setup.md) page for more details under the _Publishing "
"convention_ section."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:175
msgid "Published artifacts"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:177
msgid ""
"By default, the main binary JAR, a sources JAR, and a API documentation JAR "
"are published. You can declare other types of artifacts to publish and "
"disable or modify the default artifacts. See the [Artifact](./artifact.md) "
"page for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:182
msgid "Version scheme"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:184
msgid "`versionScheme` setting tracks the version scheme of the build:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:187
msgid "\"early-semver\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:190
msgid ""
"The supported values are `\"early-semver\"`, `\"pvp\"`, `\"semver-spec\"`, "
"and `\"strict\"`. sbt will include this information into `pom.xml` and "
"`ivy.xml` as a property."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:193
msgid ""
"`Some(\"early-semver\")`: Early Semantic Versioning that would keep binary "
"compatibility across patch updates within 0.Y.z (for instance 0.13.0 and "
"0.13.2). Once it goes 1.0.0, it follows the regular Semantic Versioning "
"where 1.1.0 is bincompat with 1.0.0."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:194
msgid ""
"`Some(\"semver-spec\")`: Semantic Versioning where all 0.y.z are treated as "
"initial development (no bincompat guarantees)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:195
msgid ""
"`Some(\"pvp\")`. Haskell Package Versioning Policy where X.Y are treated as "
"major version."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:196
msgid "`Some(\"strict\")`. Requires exact match of version."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:198
msgid ""
"This information will be annotated into the `pom.xml` file, which helps "
"downstream projects determine whether a version conflict is safe to resolve "
"or not. See [Preventing version conflicts with versionScheme](https://"
"www.scala-lang.org/blog/2021/02/16/preventing-version-conflicts-with-"
"versionscheme.html) (2021)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:202
msgid "Modifying the generated POM"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:204
msgid ""
"When `publishMavenStyle` is `true`, a POM is generated by the `makePom` "
"action and published to the repository instead of an Ivy file. This POM file "
"may be altered by changing a few settings. Set `pomExtra` to provide XML "
"(`scala.xml.NodeSeq`) to insert directly into the generated pom. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:214
msgid ""
"There is also a `pomPostProcess` setting that can be used to manipulate the "
"final XML before it is written. It's type is `Node => Node`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:223
msgid ""
"`makePom` adds to the POM any Maven-style repositories you have declared. "
"You can filter these by modifying `pomRepositoryFilter`, which by default "
"excludes local repositories. To instead only include local repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-publish.md:230
msgid "\"file:\""
msgstr ""
